{"author":{"uri":{"label":"https://itunes.apple.com/us/reviews/id1171414520"}, "name":{"label":"actual_literal_death"}, "label":""}, "updated":{"label":"2026-06-19T22:24:48-07:00"}, "im:rating":{"label":"3"}, "im:version":{"label":"4.27.0"}, "id":{"label":"14203995887"}, "title":{"label":"just as advertised, peek through the paywall, used gen ai"}, "content":{"label":"it seems that only one of each category for questions & activities is available to non-premium users (totaling to 9 sets of questions/activities). as it is, Couples Joy is basically a demo without climbing over a tall paywall. and i hate to sound like a snob but i really did not appreciate the usage of solely ai-generated assets in the Our Dream Home activity. i feel that with the amount that the subscription is pushed, Couple Joy should be able to afford some real pictures. speaking of which, for this reason i have no intentions to subscribe to the premium edition despite how limited the free version is. however, i do still like the widgets (of few that are available for free) and i like the photo sharing feature because it doesn’t make photos disappear over time in the free version, unlike the other long distance couples app i’ve tried. i will continue using the app because there are at least daily activities to do. \n\nCouples Joy is a great way to keep in touch with a long distance partner, especially those with busier schedules that make it harder to spend quality time together. it’s a pretty neat avenue for checking in daily and sharing a bit with one another, even if not at the same time.", "attributes":{"type":"text"}}, "link":{"attributes":{"rel":"related", "href":"https://itunes.apple.com/us/review?id=1624758651&type=Purple%20Software"}}, "im:voteSum":{"label":"0"}, "im:contentType":{"attributes":{"term":"Application", "label":"Application"}}, "im:voteCount":{"label":"0"}}, 
